redfin 1214: AKS extended lock state 7 (InBioUnlock) after a Touch ID unlock, kern.sweet_passcode_biostate (default 0)

SpringBoard only acts on a Touch ID unlock through SBUIBiometricResource's "bio unlocked" event (4), which it
raises when the keybag reports authenticated with extended lock state 7. We reported 0 at once, so the passcode
pad never autofilled/unlocked after a match and no success feedback was played. With the switch on, sel 35 reports
7 until SpringBoard confirms with aks_unlock_device without a passcode (MKBUnlockDevice(nil)), a lock, or 30 s.
A nil-passcode unlock while locked is refused and not counted as a wrong passcode.

